src/vendor/mir/ is the files listed in tools/mir-files.txt, copied from the
fork at the fork commit above. That commit is the upstream commit plus
exactly the patches listed, one commit each (design D12): the fork's master
mirrors upstream, its zumir branch carries the series on the upstream pin,
and each patch also sits alone on a fix/ branch cut from master, to become
an upstream pull request. tools/vendor.sh copies the tree; tools/verify-vendor
re-derives it and fails on any other difference (vendor.yaml runs it).
tools/mir-abi.txt holds the enums and structs of the vendored mir.h, the
part a consumer of the C API compiles in (design D21).

A commit, not a release, is pinned on purpose (design D2): the only tag
misses two and a half years of fixes. Every bump re-runs the spike's checks.

The patches, with the fork branch that carries each one alone:

  ea7f1643  item_name_ptr() returns after mir_assert (FALSE); three hash
            probes initialise every reg_desc_t field. Rtools gcc 14
            -Wreturn-type and -Wuninitialized. fix/rtools-gcc-warnings;
            upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  773a4834  VirtualFree (addr, 0, MEM_RELEASE). fix/windows-virtualfree;
            upstream issue https://github.com/vnmakarov/mir/issues/496.
  dafb8e1b  An unused variable in mir-gen.c; two set-but-unused ones on Apple
            aarch64. clang -Wall on macOS. fix/unused-variables; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  f35a0021  No `;` after the DEF_* macro invocations at file scope (97
            lines). gcc -pedantic. fix/no-extra-semicolons; upstream: not
            filed yet (#30).
  6edb5ce2  mem_page_size (void), the only empty parameter list. clang
            -pedantic -Wstrict-prototypes. fix/strict-prototypes; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  1571f134  snprintf with the destination array's size for all ten sprintf
            calls. R's compiled-code check rejects sprintf.
            fix/snprintf; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  0b8063f7  MIR_finish clears curr_func and curr_module first, so a context
            whose MIR_finish_func was left by a longjmp can be finished
            (the spike's patch 0001). fix/finish-clears-current; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  4c27a18f  MIR_init2's version check and _MIR_init's first allocation
            return NULL instead of exiting: both run before an error
            function can be installed. fix/init-returns-null; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  5803194c  The hash and reduce code load unaligned keys with memcpy and
            memcmp, not casts. UBSan "load of misaligned address".
            fix/unaligned-loads; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  1c4b1cca  struct MIR_insn's ops is a flexible array member in C (ops[1],
            same offset, in C++), sized with offsetof. gcc
            -fsanitize=bounds-strict. fix/flexible-insn-ops; upstream: not
            filed yet (#30). Changes tools/mir-abi.txt; no consumer yet.
  c65e7044  _MIR_set_code returns whether both mem_protect calls succeeded;
            _MIR_publish_code, _MIR_change_code and _MIR_update_code_arr
            report a code-memory failure through the error function (D11),
            so refused W+X memory is an error, not a SIGSEGV.
            fix/code-memory-errors; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  3e643e83  The Win64 interpreter shim spills xmm0-xmm3 for float and double
            arguments; it spilled only the integer registers, so a C
            caller's double argument read as a stale slot (x * 2 + 1 gave 1
            for every x). fix/win64-interp-float-args; upstream: not filed
            yet (#30).
  ca84f3e4  MIR_output_item's expr data case returns instead of falling
            into the function case (heap overflow writing out test13.mir).
            fix/output-expr-data; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  0068c2fd  As f35a0021, in c2mir.c: 29 DEF_* invocations at file scope
            (DEF_DLIST_TYPE keeps its `;`). gcc -pedantic.
            fix/no-extra-semicolons; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  df2df6f5  check_const_addr_p's unused check_ctx. gcc -Wall.
            fix/unused-variables; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  3762da20  As 1571f134, in c2mir.c: snprintf for all eight sprintf calls.
            fix/snprintf; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  3bfb8d45  Build options C2MIR_EXTRA_INCLUDES (headers given in memory,
            found first) and C2MIR_NO_FILE_INCLUDES (no header read from a
            file; any other is an error; __has_include true only for those
            in memory). Off by default. zumir's cfunction() reads no system
            header (D5). fix/c2mir-memory-includes; upstream: not filed yet
            (#30).
  7f6c4a03  c2mir freed with free what it allocated with MIR_malloc or
            MIR_calloc (its contexts and streams), so any allocator but the
            default corrupted the heap; macros, macro calls and #if states
            used plain, unchecked malloc. All now go through the context's
            allocator. fix/c2mir-allocator; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  f7672f28  Constant shifts folded through helpers: a negative value shifted
            left as unsigned, an out-of-range count gives 0 (or the sign).
            UBSan on c-tests, found by the fuzz harness's pre-run.
            fix/c2mir-shift-folding; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  96763195  def_symbol read an enumeration constant's attr as a decl
            ('enum { x } x;': ASan heap-buffer-overflow, c-tests
            new/issue365.c). fix/c2mir-enum-decl-spec; upstream: not filed
            yet (#30).
  b6e92b74  The generator's value numbering folds add, sub, mul, neg and
            shifts with wrapping unsigned arithmetic and counts modulo the
            width; INT_MIN / -1 is not folded. UBSan signed overflow and
            shifts on c-tests through c2mir. fix/gvn-fold-wrapping;
            upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  2ad09397  target_change_to_direct_calls reads the unaligned rel32 and the
            address slot in x86-64 code with memcpy. UBSan misaligned load
            on c-tests. fix/x86-64-unaligned-call-offsets; upstream: not
            filed yet (#30).
  55047839  The interpreter's add, sub, mul, neg (and their overflow-checking
            forms) wrap through unsigned arithmetic, shift counts are taken
            modulo the width, and loads and stores use memcpy. UBSan signed
            overflow, shifts and misaligned accesses on c-tests.
            fix/interp-wrapping-memcpy; upstream: not filed yet (#30).

Not patched, built differently instead (design §4.2):

  - exit, abort and writes to stderr are redirected to zumir by macros in
    src/zumir_mir_stdio.h, defined in the wrapper files just before MIR's
    sources; MIR's code is unchanged for it. c2mir's seven abort () calls
    and its stderr writes go the same way (src/zumir_c2mir.c), and its
    diagnostics are written to message_file, which zumir sets to the same
    sink, so c2mir needs no patch for either.
  - c2mir is compiled with C2MIR_NO_FILE_INCLUDES and zumir's prelude
    headers as C2MIR_EXTRA_INCLUDES (src/zumir_c2mir.c, src/zumir_prelude.c).
  - MIR's sources are compiled with gcc's -fno-tree-sra
    (src/zumir_mir_gcc.h), as upstream's makefile does: without it Rtools
    gcc miscompiles the interpreter.
  - The interpreter is compiled with MIR_DIRECT_DISPATCH (src/zumir_mir.c),
    a switch instead of computed `goto *`, which -pedantic reports.
  - No -fsigned-char: MIR's own tests pass with -funsigned-char on x86-64
    (2026-11-13) and on Linux aarch64, where char is unsigned, in
    tools/ci/platform.sh, so the core does not depend on it.
  - Symbols are hidden by $(C_VISIBILITY) and src/zumir-win.def; MIR's
    sources are unchanged for it.
  - On a CPU MIR does not target, and on Windows aarch64 (D25), the wrapper
    files compile nothing (src/zumir_mir.h).

Not vendored: the tests, benchmarks, llvm2mir, mir2c, the drivers
(c2mir-driver.c) and utilities, c2mir's README and figure. The README's Mozilla Public License mention is about
NanoJIT, not any MIR file.
